nd  remarkable moes pelgo  mando enters the local cantina to speak  with anyone who can provide him with  information  on the town's supposed mandalorian  resident fernando the result was pretty  disappointing  he didn't find one of his people but  rather kobvanth who was simply wearing  the armor with no ties to the creed  it doesn't take a deep knowledge of star  wars to recognize the gear as boba fett  although if you only watch the movies  and tv shows you'll have to do some  digging to learn about cobb vance  vanth made his debut in the star wars  universe in the aforementioned aftermath  novel  the book details his journey pretty  vaguely running over the broad strokes  of him receiving the armor from the  jawas  and subsequently saving freetown from  marauders and tuscan raiders  thus earning the moniker the marshall  which is why the season 2 premiere bears  that name  the mandalorian certainly picks up the  slack putting van front and center with  a series of flashbacks  to supply a bit more detail than the  book could pull off  committed as ever to his beliefs mando  refuses to allow vans to keep the  mandalorian armor since it technically  doesn't belong to him  since both of them are rational men they  come to an agreement that will service  both parties  mando can have every last piece of armor  so long as he helps van to take down  once and for all the carnivorous beast  known as the crate dragon  that's ravaged most pell go for years  they might not realize what they're  dealing with but long time star wars  fans instantly recognized the danger the  two were in  crate dragons are as old as star wars  itself first appearing in the background  of a new hope  after c-3po and r2d2 crashed land in the  middle of the dune sea  a crate dragon skeleton sits in the sand  way off in the distance  obi-wan kenobi later even mimics what  many fans assumed to be a great dragon's  howl to scare away some tuscan raiders  despite holding a constant menacing  presence 